# The four processes a Frappe site actually needs in front of real users.
#
# Copied into the bench directory by `scripts/start.sh` and run with
# `bench start --no-dev --procfile Procfile.pilot`, so bench still owns process
# supervision and signal handling — only what it starts is different.
#
# Compared with the generated development Procfile:
#
#   web    gunicorn instead of `bench serve`. `bench serve` is Werkzeug's
#          development server, which its own authors document as unsuitable for
#          production. The flags live in `scripts/web.sh`, where there is room
#          to say why each is there.
#   watch  gone. It rebuilds assets on every file change; in a pilot the assets
#          are built once, by `bootstrap.sh`, and nothing edits them afterwards.
#   others unchanged — the socket.io server, the scheduler, and one queue worker
#          covering the short, default and long queues.
web: /workspace/scripts/web.sh

socketio: bench socketio

schedule: bench schedule

worker: bench worker
